IMPORT prelude

-- Census and Statistics Act 1905 (Cth) -- when the Census is taken (s 8), how the Statistician may ask a person for information
-- (ss 10, 11), when not answering is an offence (s 14), the continuing daily offence and joinder (s 14 Note 2, ss 21, 22), false or
-- misleading answers (s 15), the penalties (ss 14, 15, 19, 20), entry to premises (s 18), the officers' secrecy offence (s 19), the
-- 99-year bar on giving Census forms to Agencies and courts (s 19A), and transfer of Census forms to the Archives with consent
-- (s 8A).
--
-- Edition: Compilation No. 9, compilation date 1 October 2020 (includes amendments up to Act No. 64, 2020), register id
-- C2020C00296, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/C1905A00015.txt (retrieved 13 October 2026 as the current
-- compilation). The scenario events fall in 2026, 2031 and 2032; any later amendment is not in this text.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement REQ-0021 in subjects/au/requirements.jsonl (priority 1), raised 3 times by the three Western
-- Australian cradle-to-grave scenarios: Chloe c049 (2026-08-10, census night, Chloe 23 and Liam 27: "Must they complete it?",
-- ss 8, 14); Jake k047 (2031-06-30, census night at his sister's, s 14); Daniel d048 (2032-06-30, a business survey from the
-- Bureau of Statistics to Jarrah: "Must a company answer?", s 14). SCOPED to the duty to answer and the offence of not answering,
-- with the definitions, conditions and exceptions needed to answer those questions, and the neighbouring protections a person
-- answering would ask about (ss 8A, 15, 18, 19, 19A).
--
-- NOT ENCODED. Arrangements with the States (s 6); the undertaking of fidelity (s 7); what the Statistician collects (s 9 beyond
-- its being a purpose) and the quarterly population statistics (s 9(2)); publication and charges (s 12); release determinations
-- (s 13) beyond their effect on s 19; appointment and delegation (ss 16, 17); former officers (s 19B); regulations (s 27). The
-- Census day is appointed by PROCLAMATION (s 8(2)), the other Census years and the classes of premises officers may enter are
-- PRESCRIBED (ss 8(1), 18(1)), and the s 10(2) requirement is made by NOTIFIABLE INSTRUMENT: none of these is in the Act, so each
-- is an INPUT. The dollar VALUE OF A PENALTY UNIT is set by the Crimes Act 1914 (not deposited): an INPUT. Who is a "person" (for
-- example whether a company is one) is not defined in this Act: an INPUT (inference: the Acts Interpretation Act 1901, not
-- deposited, would answer it). The Criminal Code provisions the notes cite (strict liability, s 6.1; evidential burden, s 13.3(3))
-- and Crimes Act s 4K (continuing offences) are not deposited.
--
-- Dates are written YYYYMMDD as numbers.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules conventions (the skill was not available in this
-- session; the finished naive encodings in subjects/sg were followed). No pipeline, no coverage table, no independent test
-- pass, no human gate. NOT for public use. See NOTES.md.

§ `Census and Statistics Act 1905 -- the duty to answer`

§§ `8 -- when the Census is taken`

-- s 8(1): "The Census shall be taken in the year 1981 and in every fifth year thereafter, and at such other times as are
-- prescribed." (2): "The Census day shall be a day appointed for that purpose by proclamation." (3): the Statistician "shall
-- collect statistical information in relation to the matters prescribed".
GIVEN `year` IS A NUMBER, `another time is prescribed for that year` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a Census is taken in the year` IF
        (`year` AT LEAST 1981 AND (`year` MINUS 1981) MODULO 5 EQUALS 0)
    OR  `another time is prescribed for that year`

§§ `10, 11 -- the ways a person may be asked`

-- s 10(2): "For the purposes of section 8, the Statistician may, by notifiable instrument, REQUIRE persons included in a specified
-- class of persons to fill up and supply ... the particulars specified in that form".
-- s 10(3) and 11(1): "For the purposes of section 8 or 9, the Statistician or an authorized officer may, either orally or in
-- writing, REQUEST a person" to fill up a form, or to answer a question.
-- s 10(4) and 11(2): "For the purposes of section 8 or 9, the Statistician may, by notice in writing served either personally or by
-- post on a person, DIRECT the person" to fill up a form, or answer a question, "within such period after the service of the
-- notice, being not less than 14 days, as is specified in the notice". s 10(5), 11(3): the notice "shall set out the effect of the
-- provisions of section 14".
DECLARE `Collection method` IS ONE OF
    `a requirement by notifiable instrument under s 10(2)`
    `a request under s 10(3)`
    `a request under s 11(1)`
    `a direction served under s 10(4)`
    `a direction served under s 11(2)`
    `no requirement, request or direction`

DECLARE Purpose IS ONE OF
    `the Census under s 8`
    `statistics under s 9`

-- Only the s 10(2) instrument is confined to the Census; every other method serves s 8 or s 9.
GIVEN `the method` IS A `Collection method`, `the purpose` IS A Purpose
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the method is available for the purpose` IF
    CONSIDER `the method`
    WHEN `a requirement by notifiable instrument under s 10(2)` THEN `the purpose` EQUALS `the Census under s 8`
    WHEN `no requirement, request or direction` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

DECLARE Approach HAS
    `how the person was asked` IS A `Collection method`
    `period specified in the notice in days` IS A NUMBER
    `the notice sets out the effect of section 14` IS A BOOLEAN
    `days since service` IS A NUMBER
    `the person has complied` IS A BOOLEAN
    `what is outstanding relates only to religious beliefs` IS A BOOLEAN

-- INFERENCE: a notice giving less than 14 days, or not setting out the effect of s 14, is read as not a direction "under
-- subsection 10(4) or 11(2)". The Act does not say what follows from a defective notice.
GIVEN `a` IS AN Approach
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `it is a direction under subsection 10(4) or 11(2)` IF
        (`a`'s `how the person was asked` EQUALS `a direction served under s 10(4)`
         OR `a`'s `how the person was asked` EQUALS `a direction served under s 11(2)`)
    AND `a`'s `period specified in the notice in days` AT LEAST 14
    AND `a`'s `the notice sets out the effect of section 14`

-- INFERENCE: a person "fails to comply" only once the period specified in the notice has run.
GIVEN `a` IS AN Approach
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the period for compliance has run` IF
    `a`'s `days since service` GREATER THAN `a`'s `period specified in the notice in days`

§§ `14 -- failure to answer questions`

-- s 14(1): "A person commits an offence if: (a) the person is served a direction under subsection 10(4) or 11(2); and (b) the person
-- fails to comply with the direction. Penalty: One penalty unit." (2): strict liability. Note 2: "A person commits an offence in
-- respect of each day until the person complies with the direction". (3): "Subsection (1) does not apply in relation to a person's
-- failure to answer a question, or to supply particulars, relating to the person's religious beliefs." (the defendant bears an
-- evidential burden).
--
-- A requirement by notifiable instrument (s 10(2)) or a request (ss 10(3), 11(1)) is not a "direction under subsection 10(4) or
-- 11(2)": not complying with one is not an offence under s 14.
GIVEN `a` IS AN Approach
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person commits an offence under section 14` IF
        `it is a direction under subsection 10(4) or 11(2)` `a`
    AND `the period for compliance has run` `a`
    AND (NOT `a`'s `the person has complied`)
    AND (NOT `a`'s `what is outstanding relates only to religious beliefs`)

-- s 21: the obligation "continues, notwithstanding that that period has expired ... until that act or thing is done". INFERENCE:
-- one offence for each day after the period has run, counted to the day asked about.
GIVEN `a` IS AN Approach
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the number of daily offences under section 14` IS
    IF `the person commits an offence under section 14` `a`
    THEN `a`'s `days since service` MINUS `a`'s `period specified in the notice in days`
    ELSE 0

-- s 22(1): charges for offences against s 14 "may be joined ... if those offences relate to a failure to do the same act or thing";
-- (2) one penalty may be imposed, but it "shall not exceed the sum of the maximum penalties" for each offence separately.
GIVEN `a` IS AN Approach
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the joined maximum in penalty units` IS
    `the number of daily offences under section 14` `a` TIMES 1

-- The dollar value of a penalty unit is an INPUT (Crimes Act 1914, not deposited).
GIVEN `a` IS AN Approach, `the value of a penalty unit in dollars` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the joined maximum fine in dollars` IS
    `the joined maximum in penalty units` `a` TIMES `the value of a penalty unit in dollars`

§§ `15 -- false or misleading statements`

-- s 15: a person commits an offence if (a) the person "is required, requested or directed to fill up and supply particulars under
-- subsection 10(2), (3) or (4)" or "is requested or directed to answer a question under subsection 11(1) or (2)"; (b) makes a
-- statement or provides a document in connection with it; and (c) "knows that the statement or information is false or
-- misleading in a material particular". Penalty: 10 penalty units.
--
-- Unlike s 14, s 15 reaches every method, including the Census instrument and a mere request.
GIVEN `the method` IS A `Collection method`, `made a statement or provided a document` IS A BOOLEAN, `knew it false or misleading in a material particular` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person commits an offence under section 15` IF
        (NOT (`the method` EQUALS `no requirement, request or direction`))
    AND `made a statement or provided a document`
    AND `knew it false or misleading in a material particular`

§§ `14, 15, 19, 20 -- maximum penalties`

-- s 14: one penalty unit. s 15: 10 penalty units. s 19(1), (3): "120 penalty units or imprisonment for 2 years, or both". s 20(1):
-- offences other than s 19 are prosecuted summarily; (3) a s 19 offence heard summarily: "imprisonment for a period not exceeding
-- 12 months or a fine not exceeding 20 penalty units, or both".
DECLARE Offence IS ONE OF
    `failing to comply with a direction (s 14)`
    `a false or misleading statement (s 15)`
    `an officer divulging information, on indictment (s 19)`
    `an officer divulging information, heard summarily (s 19, s 20(3))`

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the maximum fine in penalty units` IS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `failing to comply with a direction (s 14)` THEN 1
    WHEN `a false or misleading statement (s 15)` THEN 10
    WHEN `an officer divulging information, on indictment (s 19)` THEN 120
    WHEN `an officer divulging information, heard summarily (s 19, s 20(3))` THEN 20

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the maximum imprisonment in months` IS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `an officer divulging information, on indictment (s 19)` THEN 24
    WHEN `an officer divulging information, heard summarily (s 19, s 20(3))` THEN 12
    OTHERWISE 0

§§ `18 -- powers of entry`

-- s 18(1): the Statistician or an authorized officer "may, at all reasonable times, enter any premises included in a prescribed class
-- of premises" to supply or collect forms and make inquiries. (2): premises means premises other than "(a) a dwelling-house
-- (including a flat or home unit); or (b) a part of any other premises that is separately occupied or used for the purposes of the
-- residence or sleeping accommodation of a person or persons".
DECLARE Premises IS ONE OF
    `a dwelling-house`
    `a flat or home unit`
    `a separately occupied room used for sleeping accommodation`
    `a business office`
    `a shop`

GIVEN `the premises` IS A Premises, `the premises are in a prescribed class` IS A BOOLEAN, `at a reasonable time` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an authorized officer may enter` IF
        `the premises are in a prescribed class`
    AND `at a reasonable time`
    AND CONSIDER `the premises`
        WHEN `a dwelling-house` THEN FALSE
        WHEN `a flat or home unit` THEN FALSE
        WHEN `a separately occupied room used for sleeping accommodation` THEN FALSE
        OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `19 -- secrecy`

-- s 19(1): an offence if the person "is, or has been, the Statistician or an officer" and "divulges or communicates to another
-- person (other than the person from whom the information was obtained) any information given under this Act". (2): not if "(a) in
-- accordance with a determination under section 13; or (b) for the purposes of this Act".
GIVEN `is or was the Statistician or an officer` IS A BOOLEAN, `divulged to someone other than the person it came from` IS A BOOLEAN, `under a section 13 determination` IS A BOOLEAN, `for the purposes of this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the officer commits an offence under section 19` IF
        `is or was the Statistician or an officer`
    AND `divulged to someone other than the person it came from`
    AND (NOT `under a section 13 determination`)
    AND (NOT `for the purposes of this Act`)

§§ `19A -- the 99-year bar`

-- s 19A(1), (2): the Statistician or an officer "must not, at any time during the period of 99 years beginning on the Census day for
-- a Census" be required to divulge, or voluntarily give, information in a Census form to an Agency, or to a court or tribunal
-- (Agencies: "other than in accordance with this Act"). (3): "Census day ... means the day appointed, under subsection 8(2)".
-- INFERENCE: the period beginning on the Census day ends on the day before its 99th anniversary (29 February not handled).
GIVEN `the Census day` IS A NUMBER, `the date asked about` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Census form is protected from Agencies and courts` IF
        `the date asked about` AT LEAST `the Census day`
    AND `the date asked about` LESS THAN `the Census day` PLUS 990000

§§ `8A -- transfer to the Archives`

-- s 8A: if a form is given under s 10 "in relation to the Census taken in the year 2001 or a later year" and "a person has
-- consented, in accordance with the form" to transfer to the Archives, "the Statistician must transfer the information".
GIVEN `the Census year` IS A NUMBER, `the person consented on the form` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Statistician must transfer the form to the Archives` IF
    `the Census year` AT LEAST 2001 AND `the person consented on the form`
